module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "list_typed_value_element_mismatch_admitted" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value whose type is List<T> reaches a position declared List<U> with T and U established and distinct, and the program is Accepted. HARM: silent wrongness at the compiler floor. DESIGN section 4b names `values inhabit declared types` as ordinary floor, so this sits below it until the pair is refused before execution. The value fails later inside a String primitive or a persisted record that expected assignment text.",

    "HOW IT SURFACED (srv1 workspace bring-up, ledger F19/F36, operator plan 2026-10-13 restore trust in compiler and emitter boundaries). Confirmed production path: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator dispatch_worker_unit_properties_for_plan returns List<SystemdRunProperty>; a caller of gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_session_placement session_placement_record_write declared unit_properties: List<String>. The typecheck reported 0 blocking errors; it failed at runtime. The live caller on current main already maps through extdeps.systemd.systemd_run systemd_run_property_assignment; that conversion is the accepted positive control, not a license for the raw list.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is NOT a list LITERAL whose element fails (that position was already judged; test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_direct_call_witness w_wrong_element_type_in_a_list_at_a_direct_call_argument_is_refused). It is NOT product-at-a-bare-scalar-formal (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted): both sides are List applications. The F19/F36 receipt on that class said list element types were not established as unchecked because v1.compiler.infer direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags exists; this class is the missing execution of that arm on the production pair. It is NOT Wrapper<KindA> versus Wrapper<KindB> (already refused): the production pair is a kernel String type argument against a nominal product.",

    "THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (DESIGN section 6b). The seed already constructs PositionGenericTypeArgument obligations for aligned List applications whose type-argument identities are known (direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags) and hands each child pair to declared_type_obligation_diags. After gunbc#13391, product_at_scalar_declared_type refuses a product at a kernel String. Measured on main bd509bb84e7 by `gunbc compile` of a one-module fixture matching the production shape (`fn write(unit_properties: List<String>)`, `fn props() -> List<RunProp>`, `write(unit_properties: props())`): exit 1, blocking `value does not inhabit its declared type at the generic type argument: declared 'Primitive(String)', produced 'Product(RunProp)'`. The mapped conversion fixture exits 0. So the seed judgement is justified. The remaining deficit was EVIDENCE: the list-typed-value case was declared unmeasured in the list-literal witness, and no recurring_failure_mode row owned this pair. v2 owns the same judgement in v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance (exact structural equality of Instantiation nodes). The seed is not edited: a second wall in frozen seed semantics would not serve v2 self-host. The v2 relation claim is the self-host consumer.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: structurally guaranteed on the seed compile / compile_dag_diagnostic_census path (blocking DeclaredTypeNotInhabited at PositionGenericTypeArgument). NOT MEASURED on the emitted v2-native compiler judging authored source; that path is outside this change, so the class's reported rung as a whole is the minimum and stays structurally guaranteed only where measured. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Both List applications and both element identities are established; a product never inhabits String; the invalid program is authorable, so impossibility is not available. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: the emitted v2-native compiler refuses this same authored pair on its acceptance path, sufficient for the enrolled RED in test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_typed_value_witness to stay green when run through that binary, and for this row to name native as covered rather than residual.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster. Enrolled controls: test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_typed_value_witness a_list_of_product_at_a_list_of_string_argument_is_refused (RED, compile_dag_diagnostic_census) and mapping_each_product_to_a_string_at_a_list_of_string_argument_is_accepted (GREEN). v2 relation: v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_application_argument_inhabitance_witness inhabitance_list_of_product_at_list_of_int_refuses_holds.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN TWO (2026-10-25, `merry-deer-485`, node://adhoc-b4e23a71-bbd; reported by `tidy-ant-251` from a `sunny-bee-153` probe): A LIST WHOSE HEAD IS SPELLED `List` AT A FORMAL SPELLED `FreeMonoid<String>`. The probe is one fn, `fn fmj_join(xs: List<T>) -> String { string_concat_join(fields: xs, separator: \",\") }`, calling `std.algebra` `string_concat_join(fields: FreeMonoid<String>, separator: String)`. The report: zero blocking for T = Bool, NonEmptyStr, FilePath, PathSegment. Re-measured on a seed built from main 88e8991e5578, one `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root <probe root> --entry <probe> --target rust` per probe, the probe root inside the workspace on the runner (BuildBuddy invocation 70843627-643a-4e04-98f0-ad3492e54ce2; the probes are not in the corpus). ACCEPTED, exit 0, no blocking row: T = std.integer `Int`, `std.types` `NonEmptyStr`, the literal `[true, false]`, and the controls T = String and `[\"a\", \"b\"]`. Likewise T = `std.types` `Bool`, `FilePath` and `PathSegment`, re-run one at a time on the same seed (invocation 3fb1e59a-02f2-49c4-aeb3-48166765f543; run nine at once, three were OOM-killed, exit 137, and are not counted from that run). Of these, the wrong-type acceptances are Bool, Int and the Bool literal; NonEmptyStr, FilePath and PathSegment are refinements of String, whose acceptance the next receipts do not count as a seed correction. REFUSED, so the call seam runs on these fixtures: the same call with a `Bool` parameter at `separator: String`, `type mismatch: expected 'Primitive(String)', got 'Coproduct(Bool)'`. Every probe also carries one advisory located inside `std.algebra` itself (a generic formal at parameter `item`), present on the String controls too, so it is not this pair's judgment. HARM: the wrong-element list reaches a String primitive and fails at run time, or rustc refuses the emitted crate.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN TWO, per DESIGN section 6b, and A CORRECTION TO THE BOUNDARY RECEIPT ABOVE. That receipt called the seed judgement justified; it is justified only for pairs whose two heads are SPELLED alike. `v1.compiler.infer` `direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags` builds its PositionGenericTypeArgument obligations only when `authored_name_at(formal) == authored_name_at(actual)`; the formal here is authored `FreeMonoid<String>` and the actual `List<T>`, and `std.types` `List<element> = FreeMonoid<element>` is a transparent alias, so the two name one type while the guard reads two spellings, builds no obligation, and the call reaches no judgment at all. The earliest unjustified link is that guard: alignment of two applications is a fact of their DECLARATIONS after alias unfolding, never of their spelling (the alias-identity family named in DESIGN section 6b, root generalization). FORK CENSUS, the same guard in the seed: `container_element_nominal_brand_mismatch` (same module) also requires equal authored names, so its element brand check is skipped on the same pair. No other judgment in `v1.compiler.infer` compares two applications' heads by authored name. NOT REPAIRED IN THE SEED (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing purpose test): no v2 self-host path depends on the seed admitting these pairs, since the native route refuses them (next receipt), so a v1 edit would serve no v2 program. The rung receipt above is therefore read with a narrower population: structurally guaranteed on the seed for same-spelled List applications; below the ladder (silent wrongness) on the seed for an alias-spelled pair whose element types are distinct and unrelated.",

    "CORRECTION FOR SPECIMEN TWO, PER DESIGN SECTION 7 (the seed is a regression oracle, never a specification). THE v2 ROUTE JUDGES WHAT THE SEED SKIPS, through its one obligation producer: `v2.compiler.infer` `infer_declared_type_obligation` presents both sides through `infer_type_alias_normalized_at`, which unfolds transparent aliases at the head and inside every Instantiation argument, so `List<Bool>` reaches `v2.std.inhabitance` `declared_type_inhabitance` as `FreeMonoid<Bool>` and the exact structural comparison decides it. No sibling check exists to generalize: the only other DeclaredTypeObligation built in infer is match coverage, which compares one declaration with itself. ROUTE CLAIMS, `v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_free_monoid_element_inhabitance_witness` (inline source through module_roots_from_source_root_ingest and resolve_in_context, then infer), all ten PASS under `claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2` on BuildBuddy at 5cbc7fef4270 inside a bound memory cgroup (`memory.max` 40000000000, `oom_kill 0`; invocation 31554c25-04a6-41c5-b993-a18d385c0221, 2026-10-25); the witness module is unchanged after that revision. SEED CORRECTIONS, refused `application_argument_does_not_inhabit`: `fmj_a_list_of_bool_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds`, `fmj_a_list_of_int_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds` and `fmj_a_bool_list_literal_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds`, each refused at the `fields` argument (the refusal's correction names that parameter). CONTROLS: `fmj_a_list_of_string_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_is_accepted_and_decided_holds` and `fmj_a_list_of_a_transparent_string_alias_is_accepted_and_decided_holds` and `fmj_a_string_list_literal_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_is_accepted_and_decided_holds`, each accepted with EVERY diagnostic it carries in an admitted set measured on these probes (`infer_grounding_not_derived` only). Decided is established by what an accepted run may carry, not by a list of undecidable reasons to look for, which would read a reason added later as decided (fail open); the predicate's own reds, `fmj_an_undecided_return_is_not_read_as_decided_holds` and `fmj_a_generic_return_is_not_read_as_decided_holds`, are two modules v2 accepts while counting an obligation undecided, and the predicate refuses both. NOT SEED CORRECTIONS -- PINS OF v2's CURRENT FAIL-CLOSED READING: `fmj_a_list_of_a_string_refinement_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds` (`NonEmptyStr`) and `fmj_a_list_of_a_two_step_refinement_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds` (`PathSegment`-shaped). A refinement of String does inhabit String, so admitting `List<NonEmptyStr>` at `FreeMonoid<String>` could be a sound covariant widening, and the seed's acceptance of it is not shown wrong (its defect there is that it judged nothing). v2 refuses because no declared route admits a refinement under an application: `declared_type_inhabitance_declared_carrier` widens a produced refinement one step at the TOP of the produced type only. THE TWO PINS HAVE DIFFERENT TRIGGERS, named as capabilities, because the relation widens ONE refinement step. The NonEmptyStr pin (`NonEmptyStr -> String`, one step) retires on a declared covariance route for refinements under List/FreeMonoid (a conversion under DESIGN section 4). The PathSegment pin (`PathSegment -> NonEmptyStr -> String`, two steps) retires only when that covariance widens along the FULL refinement-carrier chain: transitive refinement widening, which `declared_type_inhabitance_declared_carrier` does not do even at the top level today. A one-step covariance would admit `List<NonEmptyStr>` and still refuse `List<PathSegment>`, so it retires the first pin and not the second. FilePath (`String where string_non_empty`) is one step, with NonEmptyStr. Each pin turns red on purpose when its own trigger lands and is rewritten as an accepted control. THE NATIVE ROUTE OVER THE REAL CORPUS, the pairing reading for the supplied fixtures above (DESIGN section 3, a witness discriminates at one interface): at main 88e8991e5578 on BuildBuddy (invocation 443b0790-f758-4831-b035-accb3c871598), the seed built, `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped` emitted and cargo-built the native driver, and that binary ran `census-scoped //gunbc/<probe>:all dag src/v2` per probe, the probes copied into `dag/gunbc/` on the runner and calling the real `std.algebra` `string_concat_join`. Each probe imports `List` from `std.types`, as the corpus does: the bare spelling the seed admits is unbound on the native route and refuses at resolve, which is a different stage and was not counted (a first run that kept it read as no verdict at all). REFUSED at infer, `outcome: infer_refused`, `fatal_reason: application_argument_does_not_inhabit`, one refused member per closed scope and that member the probe: T = Bool, Int, NonEmptyStr, FilePath, PathSegment, the literal `[true, false]`, and the scalar Bool-at-`separator` control. ACCEPTED, no infer-refused member: T = String and `[\"a\", \"b\"]`; their scopes carry the same `std.*` advisories as the reds' (std.algebra's own generic formals), none at the probe. No seed repair, per gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing: a v2 module depending on the seed admitting these pairs would be refused by the route measured here.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "direct_call_generic_type_argument_inhabitance_diags", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.inhabitance", decl_name: "declared_type_inhabitance", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_typed_value_witness", decl_name: "a_list_of_product_at_a_list_of_string_argument_is_refused", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.declared_type_inhabitance_list_typed_value_witness", decl_name: "mapping_each_product_to_a_string_at_a_list_of_string_argument_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "container_element_nominal_brand_mismatch", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_type_alias_normalized_at", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.inhabitance", decl_name: "declared_type_inhabitance_declared_carrier", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_free_monoid_element_inhabitance_witness", decl_name: "fmj_a_list_of_bool_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_refuses_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_free_monoid_element_inhabitance_witness", decl_name: "fmj_a_list_of_string_at_a_free_monoid_of_string_is_accepted_and_decided_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
